      children: "The Facebook Conversions API (CAPI) represents a paradigm shift from client-side to server-side event tracking. Rather than relying on browser pixels to fire HTTP requests to Meta's servers, CAPI enables your application backend to transmit conversion events directly via authenticated server-to-server communication. This architectural change restores tracking fidelity, improves event match quality, and provides deterministic attribution that survives cookie restrictions. For organizations serious about ad performance optimization, implementing CAPI is no longer optional-it's a technical necessity that directly impacts bottom-line metrics."
